  "rewrites": {
   "2": {
    "original": "If a social enterprise fails, its wholesale collapse may prove a healthy and rewarding experience for the entrepreneurs involved, but the social assets built up over the vehicle\u2019s lifespan would remain intact, if indeed they are in any way transferable.",
    "rewrite": "Should a social enterprise fall apart, an overall breakdown might still provide rewarding insights for the founders. Meanwhile, the social assets accumulated during the venture could potentially survive, provided they can be transferred somehow."
   },
   "1": {
    "original": "Part of the challenge for CG Nepi this is buried not just in finding a way of measuring Return on Social Investment, but actually using that to show successes according to the expectations of the many tribes on which we depend.",
    "rewrite": "The challenge for CG Nepi lies not only in developing a method to measure Return on Social Investment, but also in employing it to demonstrate success as expected by the diverse groups it relies on."
   },
   "3": {
    "original": "The asset here lies in the intellectual capital and common sense of good three or four year old business.",
    "rewrite": "The key asset resides in the intellectual capital and practical wisdom of well-established three to four-year-old businesses."
   }
  },
  "final_span": "Return on Social Investment. The challenge for CG Nepi lies not only in developing a method to measure Return on Social Investment, but also in employing it to demonstrate success as expected by the diverse groups it relies on.\nShould a social enterprise fall apart, an overall breakdown might still provide rewarding insights for the founders. Meanwhile, the social assets accumulated during the venture could potentially survive, provided they can be transferred somehow. The key asset resides in the intellectual capital and practical wisdom of well-established three to four-year-old businesses.\nI\u2019ve written about what my impression of the \u201cpublic sector versus private sector\u201d view is, and it\u2019s one that\u2019s both simplistic and arrogant. The Plain English Campaign, where the new business is located, is proud of that and it\u2019s a key part of its business plan",
